yet, we recommend that you do that now.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deleted\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-22\nValid as Of: 2024-06-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2824 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.16.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:      For the Telemetry Kubernetes API (CRD), we've aligned the status conditions, so that all reasons are named consistently (#1038).      The Telemetry module is now visualized in the Kyma Dashboard (#1092).      Metrics: Metrics provided using a MetricPipeline input now have a well-defined OTEL instrumentationScope attribute defined to identify the Telemetry module's input as origin of the metric, like io.kyma-project.telemetry/prometheus (#973).      Logs: Update of Fluent Bit to version 3.0.3 (#1027).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-21\nValid as Of: 2024-06-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2825 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.16.1\nDescription: The new version addresses vulnerability CVE-2024-4323 by updating Fluent Bit to version 3.0.4 (#1113).  All SAP BTP, Kyma runtime clusters are updated automatically; no customer action required.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-05-23\nValid as Of: 2024-06-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2826 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New HTTP Header for mTLS Authentication\nDescription: We added a new HTTP header X-SSL-Client-Root-CA-DN for all requests to SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry runtime that include optional or required client certificate authentication via mutual TLS (mTLS). You can use the new HTTP header to identify the root certificate authority (CA) at the top of the public key infrastructure hierarchy with the CA that signed the client certificate.  Action:  Check whether the total amount of HTTP headers in each of your requests is still under the limit of 101 (see SAP BTP-Specific Configurations), considering that the platform now takes up an additional HTTP header.  For general information about HTTP headers that the platform uses for mTLS authentication, see SAP Note 3472521 .\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-03\nValid as Of: 2024-06-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2827 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Selected models from Amazon and Anthropic are supported via AWS Bedrock.  For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-03\nValid as Of: 2024-06-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2828 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Selected models from Meta are supported.  For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-06-03\nValid as Of: 2024-06-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2829 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Selected models from Amazon and Anthropic are supported via AWS Bedrock.  For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 202", "06-03\nValid as Of: 2024-06-03\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2829 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Selected models from Amazon and Anthropic are supported via AWS Bedrock.  For more information,